Homepage: https://github.com/sppidy/shellfleet
Description: Agent for ShellFleet: connects a host to a ShellFleet server over WebSocket and
 exposes systemd service control, terminal, and config editing.
 Agent for ShellFleet. Connects a Linux host to a ShellFleet server over a
 TLS WebSocket and exposes systemd service control, an interactive terminal,
 and remote read/write of configuration files. Pairing happens through the
 server's device-auth flow; the resulting rotating credential set is cached
 under /var/lib/shellfleet-agent/. Native installs and upgrades without a
 recorded choice use root-equivalent managed mode so host controls work;
 shellfleet-agent-mode can select the capability-free restricted posture.

